1
00:00:00,440 --> 00:00:01,670
(All people, incidents,
and backgrounds...)

2
00:00:01,670 --> 00:00:03,140
(in this drama are fictitious
and unrelated to reality.)

3
00:00:03,140 --> 00:00:04,240
(Also, children were filmed
under production guidelines.)

4
00:00:04,740 --> 00:00:06,480
That model must have been popular
back in the day.

5
00:00:06,480 --> 00:00:07,480
(Episode 34)

6
00:00:14,220 --> 00:00:16,020
Actually, a few days ago,

7
00:00:16,520 --> 00:00:18,760
I saw an identical one at my house.

8
00:00:20,360 --> 00:00:21,630
An identical one?

9
00:00:22,160 --> 00:00:24,530
Yes, it was definitely
the same model.

10
00:00:26,360 --> 00:00:28,200
It's a vintage lighter,
so I guess that makes sense.

11
00:00:31,170 --> 00:00:34,340
It must have been a model
that everyone wanted back then.

12
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:04,100
Next time,
we should invite So Yeon to join us.

13
00:01:04,570 --> 00:01:05,870
I've always thought about it,

14
00:01:05,940 --> 00:01:08,170
but we've never had
a proper meal together.

15
00:01:08,740 --> 00:01:11,380
I'll book a nice place in advance.

16
00:01:11,680 --> 00:01:12,810
Is that okay with you, Chief Cha?

17
00:01:13,080 --> 00:01:14,080
Yes.

18
00:01:14,180 --> 00:01:16,580
Just let me know in advance,
and I'll clear my schedule.

19
00:01:17,380 --> 00:01:20,420
I doubt we'll have time for that
anytime soon.

20
00:01:21,620 --> 00:01:24,520
You'll be busy
with the new scholarship program.

21
00:01:25,190 --> 00:01:26,260
And Chief Cha,

22
00:01:26,790 --> 00:01:28,330
isn't this your busiest time
right now?

23
00:01:29,530 --> 00:01:32,200
Even if we're busy,
we still have to eat.

24
00:01:32,530 --> 00:01:33,900
Why would we gather...

25
00:01:34,500 --> 00:01:35,770
when things are this hectic?

26
00:01:37,200 --> 00:01:38,500
We'll revisit the idea...

27
00:01:39,040 --> 00:01:40,470
when we're less busy.

28
00:02:05,130 --> 00:02:07,100
Mr. Seok Jin, have some fruit.

29
00:02:07,400 --> 00:02:09,100
I'll be right out
after I change my clothes.

30
00:02:10,640 --> 00:02:13,570
Why is that here?

31
00:02:13,810 --> 00:02:16,170
Oh, this?
I found it on your bedroom floor.

32
00:02:16,270 --> 00:02:17,280
This is Dad's, right?

33
00:02:17,580 --> 00:02:19,510
What? No way.

34
00:02:20,210 --> 00:02:22,650
Hubby didn't smoke,

35
00:02:23,310 --> 00:02:24,920
and he didn't like lighters.

36
00:02:26,150 --> 00:02:27,520
Then whose is this?

37
00:02:30,050 --> 00:02:31,820
I don't know.

38
00:02:32,190 --> 00:02:35,360
Hubby was holding it tightly
in his hand.

39
00:02:36,160 --> 00:02:38,630
Anyway, I hate that thing.

40
00:02:39,130 --> 00:02:41,100
When I see it, I...

41
00:02:41,200 --> 00:02:43,570
I get so scared.

42
00:02:44,470 --> 00:02:46,140
What's there to be scared of?

43
00:02:47,010 --> 00:02:48,140
Come on.

44
00:02:48,270 --> 00:02:50,140
It's broken,
and it won't even light up.

45
00:02:50,410 --> 00:02:51,410
Just look.

46
00:02:51,840 --> 00:02:53,410
No, I...

47
00:02:53,480 --> 00:02:57,320
I don't know anything about it.
It frightens me.

48
00:02:57,720 --> 00:02:58,880
Stop it.

49
00:03:07,860 --> 00:03:09,330
Please don't tell me...

50
00:03:09,430 --> 00:03:13,300
you still won't accept Chief Cha
as your future son-in-law.

51
00:03:15,570 --> 00:03:17,200
I told you last time.

52
00:03:17,800 --> 00:03:19,500
Even if he doesn't meet
your standards,

53
00:03:19,570 --> 00:03:22,770
we should accept him
because Hae Ra likes him.

54
00:03:23,240 --> 00:03:27,350
I said we should embrace
all of Chief Cha's shortcomings.

55
00:03:27,410 --> 00:03:29,150
Is that easy for you?

56
00:03:29,780 --> 00:03:32,580
Our daughter is about to marry
a man who is beneath her,

57
00:03:32,650 --> 00:03:34,650
and you're completely fine
with that?

58
00:03:36,250 --> 00:03:37,860
Is it because I said...

59
00:03:37,920 --> 00:03:40,890
Chief Cha resembles you
when you were young?

60
00:03:42,130 --> 00:03:43,130
What?

61
00:03:43,290 --> 00:03:44,700
Am I wrong?

62
00:03:44,960 --> 00:03:48,930
You don't want to acknowledge
your past,

63
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:51,800
so you dislike Chief Cha
because he reminds you...

64
00:03:51,870 --> 00:03:53,710
of the past you want to erase.

65
00:03:54,570 --> 00:03:55,910
Are you kidding me?

66
00:03:55,910 --> 00:03:57,210
If that's not it,

67
00:03:57,340 --> 00:03:59,040
then be a little nicer to Chief Cha.

68
00:04:00,110 --> 00:04:03,880
The more you act like this,
the more it breaks Hae Ra's heart.

69
00:04:13,590 --> 00:04:14,760
A few days ago,

70
00:04:15,030 --> 00:04:17,400
I saw an identical one at my house.

71
00:04:18,430 --> 00:04:19,600
An identical one?

72
00:04:20,160 --> 00:04:22,670
Yes, it was definitely
the same model.

73
00:04:24,070 --> 00:04:25,140
Hold on.

74
00:04:25,800 --> 00:04:28,110
Is that the one I lost back then?

75
00:04:36,150 --> 00:04:38,380
- I'm home.
- Hey.

76
00:04:39,020 --> 00:04:42,150
You're making kimchi again?
You just made some a few days ago.

77
00:04:42,450 --> 00:04:43,660
I'm going to share it.

78
00:04:44,120 --> 00:04:45,120
With who?

79
00:04:45,720 --> 00:04:47,460
Think of it as employee welfare.

80
00:04:47,730 --> 00:04:49,830
I see. It's for Eun Guk.

81
00:04:50,130 --> 00:04:51,130
Yes.

82
00:04:52,230 --> 00:04:54,500
He must be really good at his job,

83
00:04:54,570 --> 00:04:56,970
seeing as you're giving him
something for free.

84
00:04:57,240 --> 00:04:59,300
- What?
- I mean, it's true.

85
00:04:59,800 --> 00:05:03,470
You don't just make kimchi
for someone.

86
00:05:04,580 --> 00:05:05,580
Well,

87
00:05:05,640 --> 00:05:08,580
it's just to encourage him
to keep up the good work.

88
00:05:09,580 --> 00:05:10,580
Really?

89
00:05:12,850 --> 00:05:13,850
Let me have a taste.

90
00:05:19,860 --> 00:05:21,030
Delicious as always.

91
00:05:24,660 --> 00:05:26,300
Eun Seol will love this too.

92
00:05:26,730 --> 00:05:29,530
- What?
- I mean, I'll help too.

93
00:05:29,530 --> 00:05:30,640
What should I do?

94
00:05:30,870 --> 00:05:31,870
Give me some red chili powder.

95
00:05:31,940 --> 00:05:33,100
Red chili powder.

96
00:05:33,640 --> 00:05:36,010
Wait, you made this yourself?

97
00:05:36,770 --> 00:05:38,210
It's no big deal.

98
00:05:39,040 --> 00:05:41,050
If you keep eating
your grandma's kimchi,

99
00:05:41,250 --> 00:05:44,050
it won't just ruin your taste buds,
it might ruin your health too.

100
00:05:44,620 --> 00:05:48,250
So, think of it as kimchi provided
for employee protection.

101
00:05:49,120 --> 00:05:51,860
Such deep meaning. Thank you.

102
00:05:52,090 --> 00:05:53,190
I'll enjoy it.

103
00:05:54,890 --> 00:05:56,660
Let me know when you finish it.

104
00:05:56,860 --> 00:06:00,000
I can easily make extra
when I make ours.

105
00:06:00,900 --> 00:06:03,070
Got it. Thank you, boss.

106
00:06:06,740 --> 00:06:08,370
When will the partner company...

107
00:06:08,440 --> 00:06:10,610
send over the revised sample
for the fabric replacement?

108
00:06:11,280 --> 00:06:12,540
I urged them,

109
00:06:12,610 --> 00:06:14,710
so it'll arrive
by tomorrow afternoon at the latest.

110
00:06:17,150 --> 00:06:18,720
- Seok Jin.
- Yes?

111
00:06:21,890 --> 00:06:25,390
You know Jae Seong
is launching a whiskey brand, right?

112
00:06:26,790 --> 00:06:28,030
Yes, I heard.

113
00:06:28,430 --> 00:06:29,790
He's having a dinner party.

114
00:06:30,460 --> 00:06:31,560
I'm guessing you're not going.

115
00:06:32,460 --> 00:06:34,200
You're uncomfortable around him.

116
00:06:35,830 --> 00:06:39,000
But I think Dad is going too,

117
00:06:39,070 --> 00:06:40,640
and it's all for business.

118
00:06:43,310 --> 00:06:44,310
Still,

119
00:06:44,380 --> 00:06:46,380
if you don't want to go,
I won't go either.

120
00:06:47,650 --> 00:06:49,050
To me, Chief Cha is...

121
00:06:49,550 --> 00:06:52,180
the general manager
of Cheongma's new brand.

122
00:06:53,350 --> 00:06:56,190
Being my future son-in-law is
something to wait and see about.

123
00:06:56,750 --> 00:06:58,290
No, I should go.

124
00:06:59,120 --> 00:07:00,120
Really?

125
00:07:01,060 --> 00:07:02,730
Your father is coming too, right?

126
00:07:02,790 --> 00:07:05,930
Yes, my dad is good friends
with Jae Seong's dad.

127
00:07:06,360 --> 00:07:08,670
It's settled then.
No changing your mind.

128
00:07:09,200 --> 00:07:10,330
Sure, let's go.

129
00:07:11,770 --> 00:07:13,700
Should we just reveal everything
this time?

130
00:07:13,770 --> 00:07:14,770
Reveal what?

131
00:07:14,840 --> 00:07:16,970
They are all people we know anyway.

132
00:07:17,040 --> 00:07:19,980
We can just officially announce
when our wedding is.

133
00:07:20,180 --> 00:07:21,710
There you go,
getting ahead of yourself again.

134
00:07:22,680 --> 00:07:24,280
Anyway, you're really going, okay?

135
00:07:31,690 --> 00:07:32,790
Darn.

136
00:07:33,790 --> 00:07:35,490
How did he find out my number?

137
00:07:36,290 --> 00:07:38,830
He likely alternated between a few
of the numbers you used to use...

138
00:07:38,900 --> 00:07:40,900
and made random calls.

139
00:07:41,630 --> 00:07:43,300
Once he heard your voice,

140
00:07:43,370 --> 00:07:45,540
he must've known it was you.

141
00:07:48,410 --> 00:07:50,640
I should've used
a completely different set of numbers.

142
00:07:51,280 --> 00:07:53,040
Even if you change
your number right now,

143
00:07:53,340 --> 00:07:55,450
if he already knows
that you changed your name,

144
00:07:55,910 --> 00:07:57,250
he'll easily find you again.

145
00:07:59,280 --> 00:08:01,950
Are you sure he doesn't know
who I've become yet?

146
00:08:02,190 --> 00:08:04,690
Yes. He seems to be asking around,

147
00:08:05,060 --> 00:08:06,520
but unless he hires people,

148
00:08:06,720 --> 00:08:08,190
it'll be difficult for him
to find out on his own.

149
00:08:10,960 --> 00:08:14,630
Is there any good way
to keep An Guk Cheol tied up?

150
00:08:16,770 --> 00:08:18,170
I have a plan.

151
00:08:20,570 --> 00:08:22,540
So that you won't have
to worry about it,

152
00:08:23,410 --> 00:08:24,440
I'll make sure...

153
00:08:25,940 --> 00:08:27,610
to handle him on my end.

154
00:08:28,480 --> 00:08:31,280
All right, I'll see how you do.

155
00:08:32,850 --> 00:08:35,690
Don't you start supporting
the scholarship program today?

156
00:08:36,220 --> 00:08:37,220
Yes.

157
00:08:37,760 --> 00:08:39,460
Neither the Chairman
nor Ko Eun Seol...

158
00:08:39,520 --> 00:08:41,760
likes people who try to show off
right off the bat.

159
00:08:42,190 --> 00:08:43,590
Read the room silently.

160
00:08:44,200 --> 00:08:46,930
Don't hastily voice your opinions
or block theirs.

161
00:08:48,130 --> 00:08:49,230
I will keep that in mind.

162
00:08:50,600 --> 00:08:53,540
Starting today,
we have one more person...

163
00:08:53,600 --> 00:08:55,640
who'll be helping us with our work.

164
00:08:55,970 --> 00:08:57,840
What? Who exactly...

165
00:08:59,140 --> 00:09:00,880
Oh, there he is.

166
00:09:01,650 --> 00:09:03,780
- Welcome.
- Hello.

167
00:09:03,920 --> 00:09:06,180
I'm Secretary Choi Jun Hwan,
here to assist you...

168
00:09:06,250 --> 00:09:07,750
with the new scholarship program.

169
00:09:08,520 --> 00:09:09,950
Have a seat over here.

170
00:09:12,320 --> 00:09:14,830
Eun Seol, is this your first time
meeting him?

171
00:09:15,790 --> 00:09:19,000
He helped me out the other day.

172
00:09:19,330 --> 00:09:20,330
I see.

173
00:09:20,330 --> 00:09:22,870
Then you two must already
know each other.

174
00:09:23,500 --> 00:09:24,640
That's great.

175
00:09:25,470 --> 00:09:28,610
Managing Director Joo's schedule
must keep you busy enough,

176
00:09:28,610 --> 00:09:29,970
so thank you so much...

177
00:09:29,970 --> 00:09:32,110
for assisting with the scholarship program
as well.

178
00:09:32,910 --> 00:09:34,180
Not at all.

179
00:09:34,180 --> 00:09:38,080
Director Joo instructed me to assist
so that your new program proceeds...

180
00:09:38,280 --> 00:09:40,890
without any difficulties.

181
00:09:40,950 --> 00:09:42,790
The program hasn't even
kicked off yet,

182
00:09:42,850 --> 00:09:45,720
but I already feel reassured
thanks to you.

183
00:09:46,720 --> 00:09:48,560
I look forward to working with you.

184
00:09:48,660 --> 00:09:49,660
Thank you.

185
00:09:57,840 --> 00:10:01,510
I had no idea I'd be planning
the scholarship program with you.

186
00:10:01,870 --> 00:10:03,070
I had no idea either.

187
00:10:03,410 --> 00:10:05,180
If I had known
we'd be working together,

188
00:10:05,240 --> 00:10:07,410
I would've volunteered
for the position myself.

189
00:10:08,650 --> 00:10:09,880
Do you mean that?

190
00:10:10,180 --> 00:10:11,250
Of course.

191
00:10:11,480 --> 00:10:13,050
I like you a lot, Eun Seol.

192
00:10:14,450 --> 00:10:16,350
You're too casual for your own good.

193
00:10:17,050 --> 00:10:18,660
This won't stand.

194
00:10:18,720 --> 00:10:20,660
I need to set you straight
as your senior.

195
00:10:20,730 --> 00:10:22,530
Well, by all means.

196
00:10:23,390 --> 00:10:27,030
I will dedicate my body and soul
to serve you, Eun Seol.

197
00:10:29,930 --> 00:10:31,440
See you at the next meeting then.

198
00:10:32,070 --> 00:10:34,210
Sure, I'll see you then, Eun Seol.

199
00:10:51,690 --> 00:10:54,590
(Head of Legal Affairs,
Seo Hyun Jae)

200
00:10:56,390 --> 00:10:58,230
For Eun Seol's retrial,

201
00:10:58,460 --> 00:10:59,830
it'd be best to look into...

202
00:10:59,830 --> 00:11:02,300
the people around
the late Manager Na.

203
00:11:07,470 --> 00:11:10,170
(Customer Service: Inquiry)

204
00:11:16,950 --> 00:11:18,620
Manager Na's daughter?

205
00:11:19,450 --> 00:11:22,220
Who presented the recent
leather flexibility test report?

206
00:11:22,490 --> 00:11:23,490
I did.

207
00:11:23,750 --> 00:11:27,220
The deviation seems too extreme
during the sampling process.

208
00:11:27,960 --> 00:11:29,890
You should cross-reference
the data with the factory...

209
00:11:30,030 --> 00:11:31,300
and review it again.

210
00:11:32,360 --> 00:11:34,530
Sure, I'll revise
and resubmit the report.

211
00:11:39,070 --> 00:11:40,600
Have you decided on the venue
for the team dinner tonight?

212
00:11:40,670 --> 00:11:42,670
I chose the pub
at the intersection nearby.

213
00:11:43,310 --> 00:11:45,310
Sounds good. Let's conclude
today's meeting here.

214
00:11:46,740 --> 00:11:48,680
- Good work, everyone.
- Good work.

215
00:11:50,350 --> 00:11:52,320
You secured
all the purchase records...

216
00:11:52,480 --> 00:11:54,820
for Chairman Kim's wife's
recent gallery event?

217
00:11:55,290 --> 00:11:58,120
Yes, I secured them
through Secretary Choi.

218
00:11:58,820 --> 00:12:01,490
It seems the newly hired secretary
is quite useful.

219
00:12:02,530 --> 00:12:03,530
Yes,

220
00:12:03,590 --> 00:12:06,060
he's perceptive
and quick on his feet.

221
00:12:06,460 --> 00:12:08,230
Tell him I'll buy him
a meal sometime.

222
00:12:10,700 --> 00:12:13,700
This should be enough evidence.

223
00:12:14,470 --> 00:12:18,810
I also made an appointment
to apologize to Chairman Kim.

224
00:12:19,980 --> 00:12:21,110
Chairman Kim.

225
00:12:21,850 --> 00:12:24,450
He said
he'd give me a pass this time.

226
00:12:27,380 --> 00:12:30,920
Who does he think he is
to forgive me?

227
00:12:32,320 --> 00:12:35,390
Take this opportunity
to firmly imprint in his mind...

228
00:12:35,760 --> 00:12:38,100
who the true owner of Cheongma is.

229
00:12:38,830 --> 00:12:40,500
That I should.

230
00:12:41,370 --> 00:12:42,770
By the way, Director Joo,

231
00:12:43,770 --> 00:12:47,610
you know Chairman Min's son,
Min Jae Seong, right?

232
00:12:48,470 --> 00:12:49,470
Yes.

233
00:12:49,740 --> 00:12:53,080
I heard he launched
a whiskey brand recently.

234
00:12:53,380 --> 00:12:54,450
Anyway,

235
00:12:55,310 --> 00:12:57,150
how about him as a match
for our Hae Ra?

236
00:12:58,480 --> 00:12:59,780
As a match for Hae Ra?

237
00:13:02,120 --> 00:13:04,920
I don't think he has
a very good reputation,

238
00:13:05,220 --> 00:13:06,920
both in business...

239
00:13:07,490 --> 00:13:10,030
and in his personal life with women.

240
00:13:10,030 --> 00:13:13,560
Well, as far as women go,
every businessman is like that.

241
00:13:14,430 --> 00:13:18,100
Above all,
he has a solid background,

242
00:13:18,170 --> 00:13:19,800
unlike Chief Cha.

243
00:13:22,140 --> 00:13:25,740
Will Hae Ra give up
on Chief Cha easily?

244
00:13:26,380 --> 00:13:27,950
For Hae Ra's sake,

245
00:13:28,010 --> 00:13:30,550
we need to create a rival
for Chief Cha.

246
00:13:31,320 --> 00:13:33,350
If he really hates what I'm doing,

247
00:13:34,050 --> 00:13:35,950
he'll walk away on his own.

248
00:14:05,150 --> 00:14:06,250
A gift?

249
00:14:06,950 --> 00:14:08,020
Yes.

250
00:14:08,620 --> 00:14:12,060
He's apologizing to Chairman Kim,
after all.

251
00:14:12,920 --> 00:14:15,660
If he takes another wrong step,

252
00:14:16,090 --> 00:14:18,800
I'm worried he'll prepare something
totally strange.

253
00:14:19,400 --> 00:14:20,530
I see.

254
00:14:21,000 --> 00:14:23,330
You know Chairman Kim's taste,
right?

255
00:14:23,570 --> 00:14:25,570
It's meant as an apology,

256
00:14:25,770 --> 00:14:29,610
so if the gift is too grand,
the sincerity gets lost.

257
00:14:30,410 --> 00:14:31,780
What would be good?

258
00:14:32,680 --> 00:14:35,710
How about honey from
a master beekeeper in Mount Jiri?

259
00:14:36,380 --> 00:14:39,920
Oh, that would be great.

260
00:14:52,760 --> 00:14:56,170
You've been flirting less lately.

261
00:14:56,730 --> 00:14:58,670
I haven't been flirting with anyone.

262
00:14:59,870 --> 00:15:01,970
Right, as if you'd know.

263
00:15:02,810 --> 00:15:06,180
People who flirt never seem
to realize they're doing it.

264
00:15:09,250 --> 00:15:10,480
But you never know.

265
00:15:10,880 --> 00:15:13,950
Who knows how liquid courage
will make you flirt?

266
00:15:16,190 --> 00:15:17,220
Ms. Kang.

267
00:15:18,460 --> 00:15:19,690
Can you hold your liquor?

268
00:15:20,060 --> 00:15:21,690
Me? More or less.

269
00:15:21,930 --> 00:15:23,330
I handle it pretty well.

270
00:15:24,030 --> 00:15:25,530
I'm saying I won't get drunk.

271
00:15:25,630 --> 00:15:27,830
Hey, I have a high tolerance too.

272
00:15:29,770 --> 00:15:32,340
I doubt you're any match for me,

273
00:15:32,940 --> 00:15:34,310
alcohol or otherwise.

274
00:15:37,370 --> 00:15:39,380
Hey, it's you who's no match for me!

275
00:15:44,880 --> 00:15:46,880
Everyone seems to be in a good mood.

276
00:15:48,220 --> 00:15:50,290
All your hard work
brought us here today.

277
00:15:50,350 --> 00:15:53,060
That goes for you, Young Ung,
and Ji Soo.

278
00:15:53,060 --> 00:15:54,430
By the way, your hair...

279
00:15:54,490 --> 00:15:56,390
- I tried slicking it back.
- Really? It's kind of too much.

280
00:15:56,460 --> 00:15:58,430
Ji Soo, nice work as well.
Help yourself to plenty today.

281
00:15:59,730 --> 00:16:01,400
Let's not get tired
for the rest of the race...

282
00:16:01,500 --> 00:16:03,500
and finish strong.

283
00:16:03,870 --> 00:16:06,100
- We can do it. Right?
- We can do it.

284
00:16:06,400 --> 00:16:07,970
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

285
00:16:07,970 --> 00:16:09,870
- Great job, everyone.
- Great job.

286
00:16:31,460 --> 00:16:34,570
Eun Seol worked the hardest.

287
00:16:35,130 --> 00:16:39,940
Right after joining the company,
the team had to launch a new brand.

288
00:16:40,070 --> 00:16:43,340
Here, have a full glass on me
and hang in there.

289
00:16:48,680 --> 00:16:50,650
You must've had a hard time
as team leader,

290
00:16:50,650 --> 00:16:52,580
guiding an inexperienced new hire.

291
00:16:53,250 --> 00:16:54,250
So,

292
00:16:55,750 --> 00:16:57,790
take a full glass from me...

293
00:17:01,360 --> 00:17:02,390
and keep your spirits up.

294
00:17:03,930 --> 00:17:05,760
Right, I should.

295
00:17:27,220 --> 00:17:30,550
That's how you become a director
at a large corporation like this.

296
00:17:30,850 --> 00:17:32,120
You can do it too, Young Ung.

297
00:17:32,220 --> 00:17:33,690
If you have questions,
come to my office anytime.

298
00:17:33,690 --> 00:17:34,890
- Got it?
- Sure.

299
00:17:41,060 --> 00:17:43,670
Why are you two drinking so much?
That's enough.

300
00:17:43,670 --> 00:17:46,900
You two really need to stop.
I think you're already pretty drunk.

301
00:17:46,970 --> 00:17:49,110
No way. Not at all.

302
00:17:49,610 --> 00:17:51,180
I'm not drunk at all.

303
00:17:51,810 --> 00:17:54,880
I'm perfectly fine too.

304
00:17:55,710 --> 00:17:56,950
How about it, Ms. Kang?

305
00:17:57,610 --> 00:17:59,220
Up for another round?

306
00:18:00,820 --> 00:18:02,790
What the heck...

307
00:18:04,620 --> 00:18:05,620
Hae Ra?

308
00:18:06,820 --> 00:18:08,360
Why did you drink so much?

309
00:18:09,030 --> 00:18:10,030
Hae Ra?

310
00:18:11,030 --> 00:18:12,360
- Hae Ra, pull yourself together.
- Don't...

311
00:18:19,570 --> 00:18:22,070
I'll get going first then.

312
00:18:22,070 --> 00:18:23,740
You're leaving?

313
00:18:25,310 --> 00:18:28,180
No way, Eun Seol,
you can really hold your liquor.

314
00:18:28,650 --> 00:18:30,950
Of course.
Drinking this much is nothing to me.

315
00:18:31,520 --> 00:18:33,420
Then, I'll see you tomorrow.

316
00:19:09,990 --> 00:19:10,990
This.

317
00:19:12,520 --> 00:19:15,060
Oh, right. Thank you.

318
00:19:16,490 --> 00:19:18,330
But in this notepad
I stumbled across,

319
00:19:19,360 --> 00:19:21,630
I noticed quite a few
familiar names.

320
00:19:22,170 --> 00:19:23,170
What?

321
00:19:24,030 --> 00:19:25,440
Familiar names?

322
00:19:34,810 --> 00:19:36,250
That day, ten years ago,

323
00:19:37,110 --> 00:19:39,120
the person who killed your mother...

324
00:19:39,780 --> 00:19:41,120
was me.

325
00:20:04,640 --> 00:20:05,640
(To Ko Eun Seol)

326
00:20:09,010 --> 00:20:12,350
Oh, no. No, it can't be.

327
00:20:13,120 --> 00:20:14,620
No way...

328
00:20:17,290 --> 00:20:18,290
No...

329
00:20:23,360 --> 00:20:25,530
(Join MU English Academy
to build your confidence!)

330
00:20:39,740 --> 00:20:41,950
Come on, please...

331
00:21:26,920 --> 00:21:29,630
Gosh, Eun Seol, are you okay?

332
00:21:30,990 --> 00:21:34,460
- Attorney Seo.
- Sit here for a second.

333
00:21:46,740 --> 00:21:48,110
What's wrong?

334
00:21:49,610 --> 00:21:50,910
I don't know.

335
00:21:54,480 --> 00:21:55,590
I'm just...

336
00:21:57,320 --> 00:21:58,990
I'm just scared of everything.

337
00:22:01,630 --> 00:22:03,830
Can the retrial even be held?

338
00:22:05,860 --> 00:22:07,060
Was Manager Na...

339
00:22:08,130 --> 00:22:10,230
really the killer?

340
00:22:12,300 --> 00:22:13,300
Am I...

341
00:22:14,710 --> 00:22:15,770
really allowed...

342
00:22:16,610 --> 00:22:18,210
to live just like...

343
00:22:19,440 --> 00:22:21,010
everyone else does?

344
00:22:23,950 --> 00:22:25,520
I just don't know.

345
00:22:33,590 --> 00:22:34,590
I understand.

346
00:22:35,760 --> 00:22:37,030
Your Daddy Long Legs...

347
00:22:38,330 --> 00:22:41,360
will protect you even more fiercely
from now on.

348
00:22:44,230 --> 00:22:45,240
Just trust me.

349
00:22:46,270 --> 00:22:48,240
Thank you, Attorney Seo.

350
00:22:54,710 --> 00:22:57,780
Her team went out for dinner today.

351
00:22:58,480 --> 00:23:02,220
The new product Eun Seol developed
is getting a great reaction.

352
00:23:03,320 --> 00:23:05,660
I guess she drank too much
while celebrating.

353
00:23:05,720 --> 00:23:09,590
This is quite a scene
for an unmarried young woman to make.

354
00:23:10,230 --> 00:23:11,530
She reeks of alcohol.

355
00:23:11,960 --> 00:23:14,200
She really poured it
down her throat.

356
00:23:14,700 --> 00:23:17,000
Still, I'm happy to see
our Eun Seol...

357
00:23:17,830 --> 00:23:18,900
this way.

358
00:23:19,870 --> 00:23:21,300
It finally seems like...

359
00:23:21,940 --> 00:23:23,870
she's living like someone her age.

360
00:23:25,280 --> 00:23:28,280
Hanging out
and having team dinners like normal,

361
00:23:28,350 --> 00:23:32,080
getting drunk
and passing out like this.

362
00:23:32,620 --> 00:23:33,720
Seeing Eun Seol...

363
00:23:34,990 --> 00:23:36,320
let her guard down like this...

364
00:23:37,250 --> 00:23:38,260
puts my mind at ease.

365
00:23:41,660 --> 00:23:42,660
Hey.

366
00:23:43,490 --> 00:23:45,230
- Does this need to be washed?
- Yes.

367
00:23:47,200 --> 00:23:48,330
What's this?

368
00:23:49,030 --> 00:23:50,470
Oh, that?

369
00:23:51,130 --> 00:23:53,270
It got on me
when I helped Eun Seol get home.

370
00:23:54,140 --> 00:23:55,670
Why did she need help?

371
00:23:55,670 --> 00:23:57,010
She had a team dinner.

372
00:23:57,670 --> 00:23:59,810
She drank too much,
so we came home together.

373
00:24:00,240 --> 00:24:01,950
Are you still hanging around her?

374
00:24:02,080 --> 00:24:05,250
Come on, you're always
hanging around Eun Guk too.

375
00:24:05,920 --> 00:24:07,350
Ko Eun Guk and I...

376
00:24:07,780 --> 00:24:11,660
have an employer-employee
relationship, unlike you.

377
00:24:12,760 --> 00:24:15,260
Who doesn't work side by side
with a part-timer?

378
00:24:16,360 --> 00:24:17,390
Okay, fine.

379
00:24:18,300 --> 00:24:20,900
Mi Rae, did I tell you this?

380
00:24:21,060 --> 00:24:22,630
- Tell me what?
- Well,

381
00:24:23,500 --> 00:24:26,270
I'll always support
whoever you date.

382
00:24:27,340 --> 00:24:29,610
- What?
- I'm just saying.

383
00:24:29,670 --> 00:24:31,840
You'll always have my blessing.
Just know that.

384
00:24:32,780 --> 00:24:33,780
Are you drunk too?

385
00:24:34,040 --> 00:24:35,050
No.

386
00:24:40,620 --> 00:24:43,320
I told you to be careful
with what you eat.

387
00:24:45,290 --> 00:24:48,060
Still, after getting some sleep,
I think it's calmed down a bit.

388
00:24:49,390 --> 00:24:51,760
Was it something I ate yesterday?

389
00:24:52,200 --> 00:24:54,630
Could it be that you ate...

390
00:24:54,660 --> 00:24:57,370
some dairy products
without realizing it?

391
00:24:59,070 --> 00:25:00,240
Did I?

392
00:25:01,570 --> 00:25:02,770
Oh, well.

393
00:25:03,270 --> 00:25:07,040
Cream-filled products
definitely contain egg whites.

394
00:25:07,640 --> 00:25:10,750
Below your neck,
does it still feel warm?

395
00:25:11,680 --> 00:25:15,050
Yes. I think I'll have to wait
and see how things go.

396
00:25:16,020 --> 00:25:17,020
Anyway,

397
00:25:17,720 --> 00:25:19,860
what should we do about
the appointment with Chairman Kim?

398
00:25:20,420 --> 00:25:21,660
What else?

399
00:25:22,190 --> 00:25:23,460
I should go alone at least.

400
00:25:24,090 --> 00:25:26,160
Will you be okay on your own?

401
00:25:26,460 --> 00:25:27,500
Or...

402
00:25:28,400 --> 00:25:29,770
Director Joo can accompany me.

403
00:25:32,440 --> 00:25:35,310
Right, Director Joo
could go with you.

404
00:25:36,540 --> 00:25:37,570
Is that okay?

405
00:25:38,540 --> 00:25:41,380
I'll prepare the gift
for Chairman Kim.

406
00:25:50,590 --> 00:25:53,120
(Planning Director, Cha Seok Jin)

407
00:25:53,190 --> 00:25:54,190
How's your stomach feeling?

408
00:25:55,290 --> 00:25:57,260
Yes, I'm feeling fine, sir.

409
00:25:57,890 --> 00:25:59,330
I think you drank a bit too much.

410
00:26:00,500 --> 00:26:02,270
Don't overdo it
at team dinners from now on.

411
00:26:03,330 --> 00:26:05,070
That's for me to manage,

412
00:26:05,640 --> 00:26:07,170
but thank you for your concern.

413
00:26:10,540 --> 00:26:11,540
Okay, you may go.

414
00:26:22,120 --> 00:26:23,150
(Customer Service: Inquiry)

415
00:26:23,490 --> 00:26:25,960
What's left to reveal
when he confessed...

416
00:26:26,290 --> 00:26:27,520
in his suicide note?

417
00:26:27,960 --> 00:26:30,090
(Cheongma Scholarship Foundation)

418
00:26:30,090 --> 00:26:32,230
(PR Director Joo Mi Ran)

419
00:26:38,840 --> 00:26:40,100
We're not in any danger right now,

420
00:26:40,970 --> 00:26:44,210
but we should be prepared
for when we're backed into a corner.

421
00:26:49,150 --> 00:26:50,710
When the investigation closes in,

422
00:26:51,750 --> 00:26:53,320
you should wrap things up here...

423
00:26:53,920 --> 00:26:55,290
and leave Korea.

424
00:26:57,050 --> 00:26:58,520
Leave Korea?

425
00:26:59,520 --> 00:27:02,360
Manager Na, you're my accomplice.

426
00:27:03,190 --> 00:27:04,430
If you keep holding out here,

427
00:27:04,930 --> 00:27:06,430
you'll end up straight in prison.

428
00:27:08,630 --> 00:27:10,270
I don't have a family to support,

429
00:27:10,900 --> 00:27:12,270
but your situation is different.

430
00:27:17,140 --> 00:27:18,140
Here.

431
00:27:20,210 --> 00:27:22,680
Write a suicide note
containing a confession.

432
00:27:23,650 --> 00:27:26,220
A suicide note?

433
00:27:27,620 --> 00:27:31,020
I'll give you 500,000 dollars
for your getaway fund.

434
00:27:49,510 --> 00:27:50,510
This is what you call...

435
00:27:51,040 --> 00:27:52,710
a perfect crime.

436
00:27:54,140 --> 00:27:56,680
Flawless and perfect.

437
00:28:30,380 --> 00:28:32,220
No wonder I had such a lucky dream.

438
00:28:35,720 --> 00:28:38,690
Let's hit the jackpot for once.

439
00:28:41,420 --> 00:28:43,390
Keep going.

440
00:28:43,590 --> 00:28:46,230
Come on. That's it!

441
00:28:46,900 --> 00:28:48,600
It's hitting.

442
00:28:49,230 --> 00:28:51,500
Let's just rake it all in.

443
00:28:52,870 --> 00:28:55,040
Keep spinning.

444
00:28:56,310 --> 00:28:57,470
Okay!

445
00:29:03,350 --> 00:29:04,510
You know,

446
00:29:05,320 --> 00:29:06,520
if there's one thing I'm sure of,

447
00:29:07,780 --> 00:29:11,320
it's that I never bring items
with an ulterior motive into my home.

448
00:29:13,990 --> 00:29:16,990
Businessmen always seem
to get it wrong.

449
00:29:17,790 --> 00:29:20,000
A large corporation should play
by the book...

450
00:29:20,200 --> 00:29:21,530
and build its foundation
on pure capability.

451
00:29:24,200 --> 00:29:25,940
But resorting to shady tricks
behind closed doors?

452
00:29:26,400 --> 00:29:27,400
Of course.

453
00:29:28,240 --> 00:29:29,540
You are absolutely right.

454
00:29:30,040 --> 00:29:32,210
A favor with such obvious intentions...

455
00:29:32,780 --> 00:29:34,740
isn't a gift. It's a shackle.

456
00:29:35,310 --> 00:29:38,280
Why would I willingly put them
around my own ankles?

457
00:29:40,380 --> 00:29:42,050
But the thing is, Chairman Kim,

458
00:29:43,120 --> 00:29:44,520
when it comes to those shackles,

459
00:29:45,290 --> 00:29:48,690
people often don't even realize
they are wearing them.

460
00:29:49,760 --> 00:29:50,890
What are you talking about?

461
00:29:51,730 --> 00:29:53,100
It's only when
the blood stops flowing...

462
00:29:53,860 --> 00:29:56,130
and the flesh rots away...

463
00:29:57,400 --> 00:29:58,400
that they finally...

464
00:29:59,300 --> 00:30:02,410
see the shackles
wrapped around their ankles.

465
00:30:10,450 --> 00:30:11,980
Director Joo, come in.

466
00:30:28,630 --> 00:30:31,330
Wait, what are you doing here?

467
00:30:33,200 --> 00:30:34,500
Do you two know each other?

468
00:30:43,510 --> 00:30:45,850
This is a modest gift
to offer my apologies...

469
00:30:46,880 --> 00:30:48,450
to you, Chairman Kim.

470
00:30:57,430 --> 00:30:58,460
(Account Transactions)

471
00:30:58,460 --> 00:30:59,500
(Purchase History of Paintings
From Chairman Kim's Wife's Gallery)

472
00:31:10,940 --> 00:31:13,010
This... Darn.

473
00:31:15,350 --> 00:31:18,550
Wait, how did you get this?

474
00:31:19,120 --> 00:31:22,090
Are your feet starting
to feel numb now?

475
00:31:23,650 --> 00:31:24,650
Those shackles?

476
00:31:25,660 --> 00:31:29,190
You put them
on your own ankles, sir.

477
00:31:29,190 --> 00:31:30,630
Are you saying...

478
00:31:31,130 --> 00:31:33,600
the two of you conspired against me?

479
00:31:34,600 --> 00:31:35,730
How dare you!

480
00:31:49,750 --> 00:31:52,450
Darn, my good luck was short-lived.

481
00:31:52,520 --> 00:31:54,280
Why did it stop coming?

482
00:31:54,320 --> 00:31:56,120
Seriously? Darn it.

483
00:32:02,790 --> 00:32:04,760
Why? What do you want?

484
00:32:07,800 --> 00:32:08,800
Darn...

485
00:32:10,370 --> 00:32:11,400
If you found a wallet,

486
00:32:11,400 --> 00:32:13,200
you should return it to its owner.

487
00:32:14,400 --> 00:32:15,840
Why you...

488
00:32:17,370 --> 00:32:19,940
You darn punk.

489
00:32:20,540 --> 00:32:21,540
Unbelievable.

490
00:32:21,780 --> 00:32:24,480
I was wrong.
I was going to return it.

491
00:32:24,550 --> 00:32:26,780
I was on my way
to the police station.

492
00:32:29,590 --> 00:32:32,060
There's still plenty of money left.

493
00:32:32,160 --> 00:32:34,190
I made a mistake, sir.

494
00:32:34,390 --> 00:32:35,860
Okay? Please spare me.

495
00:32:35,930 --> 00:32:38,460
I was wrong. I was so wrong.

496
00:32:38,930 --> 00:32:40,030
That's enough.

497
00:32:48,500 --> 00:32:49,510
Let's leave it at that.

498
00:32:49,810 --> 00:32:50,870
Who the heck are you?

499
00:32:53,980 --> 00:32:56,410
Should I call the police?

500
00:33:04,950 --> 00:33:06,290
Consider yourself lucky, punk.

501
00:33:07,390 --> 00:33:08,760
- Let's go.
- Got it.

502
00:33:18,870 --> 00:33:19,870
Are you okay?

503
00:33:21,640 --> 00:33:22,640
Yes.

504
00:33:24,210 --> 00:33:25,480
Yes...

505
00:33:46,900 --> 00:33:50,700
(A Trap Called Desire)

506
00:33:50,770 --> 00:33:53,400
You're attending
the whiskey launch event?

507
00:33:53,470 --> 00:33:54,670
Is that really necessary?

508
00:33:54,870 --> 00:33:58,310
Lately, I've been seeing
my husband a lot in my dreams.

509
00:33:58,340 --> 00:34:00,040
Ko Eun Seol, you seem to be fine.

510
00:34:00,310 --> 00:34:02,080
We were drinking cheap soju,

511
00:34:02,150 --> 00:34:03,550
so I doubt I showed
my real potential.

512
00:34:03,810 --> 00:34:05,180
You're Ko Eun Seol, right?

513
00:34:05,350 --> 00:34:07,750
Things are a bit awkward
with the CEO, right?

514
00:34:07,850 --> 00:34:10,620
So this time,
I'm not going to just let it slide.

515
00:34:10,790 --> 00:34:13,720
Everyone changes.
Is there anyone who doesn't?

516
00:34:13,790 --> 00:34:15,090
You're hiding something, aren't you?

517
00:34:15,390 --> 00:34:18,030
I was expelled
from the Women's Association.

518
00:34:18,330 --> 00:34:19,530
Honey!

519
00:34:21,100 --> 00:34:23,100
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
